  {
    "id": 2,
    "short_name": "T-PJ-003772-TAAT Clearinghouse: Re-invest to Accelerate Innovation Adoption",
    "full_name": "T-PJ-003772-TAAT Clearinghouse: Re-invest to Accelerate Innovation Adoption",
    "summary": "The Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation (BMGF) and the African Development Bank (AfDB) have been co-funding the TAAT Clearinghouse (CH) for four years, with an annual budget of approximately $2 million. This CH aims to optimize the success of national and regional agricultural investment programs by integrating the most effective technologies into these initiatives. It serves as a broker, facilitating the adoption of CGIAR-led research technologies and others, into investment projects primarily funded by AfDB. By leveraging AfDB's African Development Fund and sovereign loans, the CH promotes the deployment and scaling of vetted technologies, focusing on improving agricultural productivity and outcomes across Africa.",
    "description": "TAAT Clearinghouse: Re-invest to Accelerate Innovation Adoption",
    "start_date": null,
    "end_date": null,
    "total_budget": "3123921.00",
