  {
    "id": 3,
    "short_name": "T-PJ-003743- Technologies for African Agricultural Transformation Phase II",
    "full_name": "T-PJ-003743- Technologies for African Agricultural Transformation Phase II",
    "summary": "The TAAT Phase II project aims to drive agricultural transformation in Africa's transition contexts by strengthening National Seed Systems in selected Regional Member Countries (RMCs) through a market-based model and supporting local private sectors to scale technologies and services at the community level. Building on the successes of TAAT I, this project seeks to enhance agricultural productivity, increase household incomes and build resilient food systems by expanding access to climate-resilient technologies. This project targets raising farmers' household incomes by an average of USD 600 per annum, reaching 40 million people and significantly reducing hunger across Africa. Additionally, it will support policy reforms and regional trade through collaboration with Regional Economic Communities (RECs).",
